  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Women&apos;s Economic Resilience through Skills Training, Livelihood</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project is designed to address the pressing challenges faced by women in Warrap State, particularly in the aftermath of communal conflicts that have left communities vulnerable. The project recognizes the specific vulnerabilities of women and girls, including risks such as sexual violence and child marriage, and aims to empower them through economic means.
Given the context of internal displacement and localized conflicts in Gogrial West and Gogrial East counties of Warrap State, it is crucial to provide women with the necessary skills and resources to support themselves and their families. By focusing on entrepreneurship skills training, the project seeks to enhance women&apos;s economic resilience, enabling them to generate income and improve their livelihoods. Through a series of targeted activities such as GBV awareness campaigns and skills training in areas like kitchen gardening, bakery, hairdressing, catering, stove making, and tailoring, the project aims to equip women with practical skills that can lead to sustainable income-generating opportunities. By directly benefiting 910 women/girls and indirectly impacting 2,730 beneficiaries, the project seeks to create a ripple effect of empowerment within the community.
Above all, this project is aimed to address the immediate needs of vulnerable women in Warrap State, empower them through economic means, and contribute to their long-term resilience and self-sufficiency. By investing in women&apos;s skills and entrepreneurship, the project aims to not only improve individual livelihoods but also foster community development and economic growth in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
